cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the paper."
title: "Random walk on sphere packings and Delaunay triangulations in arbitrary dimension"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Random-Walk-On-Sphere-Packings"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper of Bou-Rabee and Gwynne on
  random walk on orthogonal tilings: convergence of the conductance-weighted walk to Brownian
  motion modulo time parametrization and of the discrete Dirichlet problem (Theorems A and B),
  their hypotheses for Poisson-Voronoi tessellations (Proposition 1.1), and a sphere packing on
  which simple random walk does not converge (Theorem 6.1). Every labelled result is proved, as
  printed or as in a corrected version of the paper. The library contains no sorry and no custom
  axiom, and each main theorem has a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: "Bou-Rabee"
    given-names: "Ahmed"
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - random walk
  - orthogonal tilings
  - Delaunay triangulations
  - sphere packings
license: Apache-2.0
references:
